[1mThe hard part was not the logic, it was the bug.[22m [38;5;10mbad()[0m passes an uninitialized [38;5;10mchar *[0m to [38;5;10mprintLine[0m (CWE-457), so the bytes reaching stdout [3mare[23m stack residue. I confirmed with the real C library that its output changes with the caller: the same [38;5;10mdriver(0)[0m prints an empty line from a shallow [38;5;10mmain[0m, [38;5;10m\xff\xff\xff\xff[0m under ctypes, and its own machine code under [38;5;10mdlopen[0m. That makes the frame geometry of every function observable, not just [38;5;10mbad[0m's — [38;5;10mgood()[0m runs at the same depth and leaves its [38;5;10m"string"[0m pointer on the exact word a later [38;5;10mbad()[0m reads.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three things were needed to match it, each found by diffing disassembly against the C:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Uninitialized C locals are materialized in real stack slots at the offsets gcc chose, with volatile accesses. Plain [38;5;10mMaybeUninit[0m reads fold to LLVM [38;5;10mundef[0m and the load vanishes entirely.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m#[inline(never)][0m plus a trailing liveness pin, and [38;5;10m-Cforce-frame-pointers=yes[0m. Without these LLVM inlined [38;5;10mprintLine[0m, used the red zone, and tail-jumped, putting the read 8 bytes off.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mdriver[0m is a naked transcription and [38;5;10mbuild.rs[0m passes [38;5;10m-z lazy[0m. The C reaches [38;5;10mgood[0m/[38;5;10mbad[0m through lazy [38;5;10mJUMP_SLOT[0m PLT entries, so its first call runs [38;5;10m_dl_runtime_resolve[0m, which overwrites the very word [38;5;10mbad[0m then reads. rustc marks those calls [38;5;10mnonlazybind[0m and there is no stable flag to change it, so [38;5;10mdriver[0m is the one function written in asm; [38;5;10mprintLine[0m, [38;5;10mbad[0m, and [38;5;10mgood[0m are ordinary Rust because the resolver only dirties stack below the caller's frame.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mVerification:[22m 24/24 differential cases byte-identical against the C [38;5;10m.so[0m — ctypes and directly-linked harnesses, one call per fresh process and long mixed sequences over a deliberately dirtied stack, including NULL, empty, and 300-byte strings, negative/non-1 [38;5;10museGood[0m, and the [38;5;10mgood()[0m-then-[38;5;10mbad()[0m residue interaction.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne case cannot be matched by any translation.[22m Under [38;5;10mdlopen[0m/[38;5;10mdlsym[0m the stale pointer aims into the library's own text. Both builds read the identical stale address — it lands on [38;5;10mbad[0m in each — but [38;5;10mprintLine[0m then prints the compiler's instruction encodings, and the string ends at a NUL inside a rip-relative displacement. Equality there requires byte-identical codegen for the whole shared object, not identical behavior. This is documented in the module comment rather than papered over.[0m[0m
